{{also|Werfen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wërfen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|werfan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*werpaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|werpan}}, {{cog|nl|werpen}}, {{cog|en|warp}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɛrfən/|[ˈvɛʁ-]|[ˈvɛɐ̯-]|[ˈʋɛʁ-]|[ˈʋɛɐ̯-]|[-fən]|[-fn̩]|[-fɱ̍]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-werfen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=3|wirft|warf|geworfen|past subjunctive=würfe}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|intransitive}} to [[throw]]
# {{lb|de|transitive|computing|[[exception]] handling}} to [[throw]]
#: {{ux|de|Der Konstruktor mit dem einen Parameter '''wirft''' in diesem Falle eine Ausnahme.|The constructor with this one parameter '''throws''' an exception in this case.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} To [[cast]]; to [[project]]
#: {{ux|de|einen Schatten '''werfen'''|t=to cast a shadow|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|ein Bild an die Wand '''werfen'''|t=to project an image to the wall|inline=1}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|intransitive}} to [[give birth]] {{qualifier|of some animals}}
#: {{ux|de|Die Sau '''wirft''' ihre Jungen.|The sow is birthing her young.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[throw]] oneself (on a bed etc.)

